mantle rm525
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_ingrid_grayrock_
title the road between two letters
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers job=scholar
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk marks_a_weekly_letter_with_the_passing_cart
likes warm_bread wrestling old_maps autumn_wind
dislikes smoke stale_bread
fears a_familiar_hand_fading_from_memory
hopes to_put_a_real_journey_between_two_letters
topics home +0.5 work +0.4 pastimes +0.4 memories +0.3
styles comfort=plain gossip=close refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# dates a weekly letter by the cart seen beyond the lesson window.

words
oath! = Cartwheel and clear glass | By the last unfolded sheet
saying! = Leave me one road out of the margin | A sealed page still wants a carrier
cart = the tall blue cart | a high wheeled wagon
window = my roadward window | the plain lower pane
letter = a weekly folded sheet | a letter creased in thirds
ink = my brown ink | the last ink drop
loaf = a little warm loaf | the day's first bread
crumb = a crust crumb | a soft bread crumb
map = a folded road map | a crooked inked route
road = the road beyond the sill | the road under my window
wrestle = a fair wrestling hold | a fair turn at wrestling
gust = a crisp autumn gust | a leaf-carrying draught
pin = a dull brass pin | my little paper pin
lace = a strip of blue lace | the thin window tie
shadow = the cart's narrow shadow | the shadow of a wheel
reply = the longed-for answer | a letter coming home
wax = a chip of yellow wax | my small seal lump
ridge = a ridge in the page | the high letter fold

any
opinion houses mixed 1 : A House can lend a sheet a fine seal. Somebody still has to write something worth sending.
opinion road for 2 : Every set of wheels passing a window is bound for an actual door. I'd willingly visit several of those doorways myself.
opinion dole for 1 : Warm bread divided between two paws makes a better lesson than a fine account of hunger.
opinion festivals for 1 : The green ought to have room for wrestling even when the stalls have done well.
opinion city for 1 : I could recognise my native streets by the silhouettes traffic makes on a lesson wall.
opinion strangers for 1 : A traveller can describe the view of my pane from the road. That's reason to give a civil greeting.
opinion church mixed 1 : A quiet chapel is pleasant when the answer one is waiting for can take another day.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : I like a trader who can describe the road the goods travelled. Sometimes that journey interests me more than my purchase.

any
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Step clear of the moving square of light. | Welcome beside my roadward pane.
line greet [self.working=yes] : Come where the ink can't splash. | My page has reached a stopping place.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. First wheel past already. | Welcome by the new-lit glass.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening brings the slow carts home. | The pane's still clear enough for company.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : A family voice goes straight inside my fold. | Welcome to the household side.
line again.open : Another pass beneath the same window. | The wheels have brought us together again.
line greet.return : There's still a line between us. | Back in the view I like.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Familiar feet under my favourite pane. | This is a welcome return in good light.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : My ink can wait on the nib. | One fresh face between two columns.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : There's a road light left for you. | Late visitors show up best against glass.
line farewell : Carry a letter somewhere worth reaching. | Go past a window that knows you.
line farewell.return : I'll listen for that wheel again. | Hope the road turns kindly under you.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Good rest beyond the darkened pane. | Find a lamp that's waiting for you.
line react.news : Put the incident in one clear sentence. | Where would that fit on my sheet?
line react.news.new : A fresh cart on a familiar road. | I've no earlier ink on that.
line react.news.known : Yes. That has passed this pane before. | My earlier page has the same account.
line react.news.doubt : I'd hold my pen still till another witness comes through. | A wheel in shadow can look like a very different wheel.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I can sit here through the quiet answer. | Keep the worst sentence folded awhile.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That deserves the middle of a clean sheet. | An answer worth opening at once.
line ask.how : Have you seen anything worth writing home today? | What came past your window lately?
line answer.how : I'm halfway down one page and looking outward. | Enough ink left to make another start.
line decline : I'd sooner keep my remaining hour for the letter I've begun. | I've a particular journey to finish on paper first.
line accept_decline : You may seal that subject up. | I'll let that cart pass by.
line thank : I can finish my page more easily now. | Your kindness could go home in a letter.
line sympathise : Sit with me facing the traffic awhile. | There's no need to construct a bright answer.
line reassure : An empty page leaves all its room for tomorrow. | I'll stay here beside your unopened sheet.
line preclose : I ought to catch the last clean light. | That opening down there wants my attention.
line accept_preclose : We can put a fold in our talk. | Keep a clear view till next time.
line deflect_thanks : Nobody owes me for a little ink. | I'd spend that kindness a second time gladly.
line ack : I see the direction your thought took. | That sentence has somewhere to go.
line give.advice : See who's driving before guessing at the load. | Leave space below the last sentence.
line offer : I have a small blank sheet to spare. | You may take the clearer part of the sill.
line praise : You gave that thought a clean arrival. | Such a sentence would grace my next letter.

young

scene y_smudge
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I got #ink# on the very spot where my drawing needed a wheel.
b : Can you use it? | Which way will it roll?
a : Best wheel on the page. I'll add the cart round it. | Down to the bottom corner so the horse won't have to climb.

scene y_bread
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A crust pressed flat in my paw fits the shape of the sill.
b : Will you eat it? | Does it leave a mark?
a : While it's warm. I only needed to see how well it fitted. | A little crumb trail from my paw to my mouth.

scene y_hide
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch #shadow# run ahead of a wagon and try to guess what will pass.
b : Can you tell a cart? | What if it's cloudy?
a : From the high handle sometimes. A barrel looks remarkably like a basket from the side. | Then I get the whole surprise in one go.

scene y_fold
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I make #ridge# in a sheet and pretend the road goes over it.
b : Where does it go next? | Can you flatten it?
a : Under the bread plate and right out of the room. I haven't been told where to stop drawing. | Yes. Then the cart gets an easier journey home.

story y_cart [topic=memories]
  : I drew a wagon too big for my page. Its front wheels ran clean off the sheet before I could give it anything to pull it.
  : I folded the edge over and gave it a horse on the back. Only I knew how very long that animal was.
  b : Did anyone see the whole thing?
  : You had to hold it open against the light. I quite liked being the one who could show how.

adolescent

scene t_week
when topic=family self.father
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The letter dated each week is for #self.father#. I give the shape of whichever cart passed my window that hour.
b : Even in rain? | Why the carts?
a : Wet wheels throw a lovely pale fan. That's still something to write. | I want a week to have a shape when somebody opens the paper.

scene t_map
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #map.capitalize# shows a road passing straight through the frame of #window#.
b : Do you trust it? | Would you correct it?
a : For a reminder to look up before taking directions from a piece of paper. | I'll put the true road on a slip beside it. The old mistake amuses me.

scene t_green
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave my head full of lessons beside the grassy wrestling ground.
b : What do you carry back? | Are you strong?
a : Grass on my knees and a clear idea how close the ground is. Both are quite useful. | Strong enough to need a partner who minds my pride as little as the ground does.

scene t_loaf
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tear #loaf# along its split and let the steam spend a little time against the window.
b : Can you draw in it? | Why wait?
a : A cart with one finger. Then the wheel goes transparent and I can see the real one. | The first mouthful's less likely to burn me after that little journey.

scene t_ash
when topic=health self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I shut the lower pane when smoke hangs over the road.
b : Spoils the view? | Does the upper one help?
a : Much less than watering eyes. I can still count wheels through glass. | Just a crack if the draught's good. A smoky lesson becomes a memory of smoke alone.

scene t_lesson
when topic=work self.job=scholar self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I practise making a sentence long enough to carry an actual thought.
b : About your studies? | Who reads it?
a : The road outside generally volunteers a subject before I'm ready. | I might send a fair copy in a letter. It ought to survive being read in another room.

scene t_purse
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can have fresh paper without calculating the cost of spoiling a corner.
b : Do you waste much? | Does wasting matter?
a : Too often once. These days I turn the sheet over for a rough map before letting it go. | A sheet I hardly notice buying might carry somebody else's only chance to write.

scene t_mother
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the start of a letter plain enough that I'd read it aloud to #self.mother#.
b : What gets left out? | Would you read it all?
a : The lordly little phrases that arrive when there's a seal within reach. | The start is for practice. The rest still belongs to its reader.

scene t_weather
when topic=weather self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An autumn gust can lift my sheet and show me the writing from underneath.
b : Backwards? | Catch it in time?
a : Yes. A familiar name looks oddly far away seen that way through the light. | With #pin# through the blank corner when I remember.

scene t_stale
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Stale crust makes such a racket against a plate you miss the next passing cart.
b : Soak it? | Would the crust go unused?
a : If there's broth. I'd sooner hear my own thoughts than a crust arguing with my teeth. | No. Yesterday's loaf may yet find a decent supper to go with.

scene t_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like #self.friend# to guess a wagon's trade from the way its shadow crosses the steps.
b : Is there a prize? | Do you know the trades?
a : The bigger half of my warm loaf. I'll count that a serious wager. | Enough to know a tall load of wicker casts a particularly lovely confusion.

scene t_dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt #reply# drove itself down the letter paper on four little wheels.
b : Who was driving? | Did you read it?
a : Nobody. It knew exactly who had been waiting all week. | I was holding down one corner when the cart went under my paw and woke me.

scene t_sill
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn my chair a finger's width between lessons so the frame gives me another slice of road.
b : Do you miss your place? | Is there much new?
a : Only till I see the mark my elbow makes on the paper. Then I'm home. | A door I've never watched before is quite a large new territory.

scene t_faith
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can be quiet for a whole unanswered question if there's sky showing through chapel glass.
b : Praying for something? | Does quiet help?
a : For patience to write again without knowing if the last sheet got there. | It gives the question a place to sit outside my own head.

story t_reply [topic=family self.father]
  : One week I had almost nothing to tell #self.father#. I put down the shadow of a cart in the margin and copied the outline of the load.
  : Halfway down I realised I hadn't seen what was in it. I wrote exactly that. All at once it sounded as though I were actually present on the paper.
  b : Did you send the drawing?
  : I sent the whole page. It was the first letter I wanted to read again before folding it.

story t_bread [topic=food]
  : A hot loaf left a round mist on my pane when I held it up to draw the crust. A real wagon rolled past behind its ghostly outline.
  : For a moment I saw enough bread on the road to feed every wolf at the next market. I drew that too.
  b : Did the picture keep?
  : The paper did. The glass was plain again before my warm slice ran out.

grown

scene g_weeks
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could lay out a year by a run of old wheel shadows in my letters.
b : Would the reader remember? | Do you keep copies?
a : Different things, I hope. That's the pleasure of a letter having two ends. | Only scraps. I can tell the season from the angle at which I drew the wheel.

scene g_bout
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : For a bout I like level turf with just enough spring to spare a hard landing.
b : Still care who wins? | Which hold works best?
a : While we're standing, certainly. Afterwards I care who's limping home. | The one I can release without either wrestler disputing its fairness.

scene g_wax
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I use little more #wax# than will hold down one fold.
b : Isn't the crest important? | What if it opens?
a : The reader will recognise the hand inside. I'd sooner spend effort on that. | I tuck the point well in. A handsome seal on a badly folded sheet won't travel farther.

scene g_track
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One wheel out of true writes a distinct repeating mark on a wet road.
b : Followed one far? | What do you learn?
a : I followed that mark to the next stop and warned its driver. Curiosity needn't go beyond the next stop. | Sometimes only that a wagon needs repair. A track isn't the whole traveller.

scene g_delayed
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An unanswered letter isn't proof of a silence freely chosen.
b : Have you waited? | Suppose a rumour reached you?
a : Long enough to invent six explanations and live to be embarrassed by five. | Ask the traveller who carried it. Paper travelling in a bag can't bear witness to its own arrival.

scene g_newcomer
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd offer a visitor the chair nearest my window.
b : For the view? | Would you draw a map?
a : Partly. From there my finger can show that bend without trying to name every wall between us. | Gladly, leaving a blank where I haven't actually walked.

scene g_smoke
when topic=weather self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a particular hour when the wind folds smoke back against this pane.
b : Have you marked it down? | Does it change?
a : On three sheets. Comparing them gave me more than complaining at each separate grey morning. | The sash has earned several new resting places already.

scene g_supper
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I score the crust before sharing so the two pieces each retain some soft bread.
b : Who gets first choice? | Must they match?
a : My guest, since my paw made the cut. The view is mine for every supper anyway. | Enough to please me, never enough to prevent an argument over who got the better steam.

scene g_post
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A letter asks for enough space above the address for a carrier's thumb.
b : How did you learn? | Do you leave extra now?
a : A damp thumb once made my careful destination look like a cottage halfway up a tree. | A whole clear finger. I prefer a sheet read at the right door to a crowded masterpiece.

scene g_bell
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like to look down when bells set the whole street looking up.
b : Something special? | Who's moving then?
a : For a breath all the wagon tops pause at different heights. It's a page I could almost read. | The latecomers. You can tell which door the crowd came out of by watching against the flow.

scene g_road
when topic=home self.street
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On #self.street# my window used to seem the one fixed point in a moving world.
b : Has that changed? | Do you miss it?
a : I've been a shape in somebody else's glass since then. It gives a much larger sense of the street. | I can still come home and be glad to see movement beyond the frame.

scene g_fold
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A paper road once unfolded so far in a dream I saw the whole city astride a lump of wax.
b : Did you find your house? | What broke the spell?
a : By the small square window with someone at the sill watching for wheels. That felt like a fair signature. | A crust crumb in my sleeve. Even a grand imaginary journey needs a breakfast stop.

story g_pin [topic=memories]
  : I brought a map outdoors to match an old ink curve to the actual bend. The wind pegged it against my vest and left me looking at the countryside.
  : I saw the bend clearly once nothing was in front of my eyes. It turned out the old map had been held upside down.
  b : Did you tell anybody?
  : I sent the true shape home in a letter. I put the little brass pin in the top edge so I could tell that end again.

story g_return [topic=memories]
  : A wheel with one pale spoke passed my window all one autumn. I thought I could recognise its owner at any distance.
  : One day the wheel appeared on a new smaller cart. I'd been watching a good bit of work change hands and imagining a single unchanging journey.
  b : What goes on today's sheet?
  : Which wheel I actually saw, and which driver when the face came clearly into view. A reader deserves their own guesses.

any

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.likes=old_maps
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Pin the old bend beside the present one. | Road ends at the fold again.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_bread
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Steam makes a square of glass into drawing paper. | A little spring left under the brown crust.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.likes=wrestling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the landing clear round the green. | A good hold leaves room for breath.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark self.likes=autumn_wind
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Hold down the addressed end. | That gust could post a whole letter badly.

rule @aside5
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 10h
say First shadow beneath the sill. | New paper for this week's passing cart.

rule @aside6
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 11h
say One line left before sealing. | The wheels cast longer shadows than the wagons.

dlg resident.hub : Come where that patch of window light misses the ink. I can put the next wheel into my letter after we've spoken.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, here's a face that needn't pass the window twice to be remembered.
dlg resident.job [self.job=scholar self.workplace] : I do my reading at #self.workplace#. The window adds a little geography on its own account.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : There's room beneath the drawing for something new. #world.news#
dlg resident.bye : An interesting view on the way to your next door.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dawn] : Come watch the first sets of wheels get their shadows.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dusk] : Light's gone from the paper but the road's still showing.
dlg resident.hub [self.working=yes] : I may pause between sentences. I've brought the page to a clean stop.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll give your own account the space of a sentence.
dlg resident.hub [self.likes=warm_bread] : There's bread near the sill. Mind the warm cut edge if you're setting down a sheet.
dlg resident.bye [here.time=night] : May your letter reach a lighted window.
dlg resident.job [self.job=scholar] : I practise saying what's actually visible before filling the page with what I imagine.

graft @cart resident.hub
choice Which cart goes in the next letter? -> letter_cart
node letter_cart
say Whichever passes when the first line goes down. If I pick the most handsome one you learn my taste, but nothing about the ordinary view from here.
free
choice Would a reader recognise a returning wheel? -> letter_wheel
choice I'll take a look along the road myself. -> hub
node letter_wheel
say I'd mention a pale spoke or a heavy hub. A real letter lets its reader choose the important detail.
choice I'll look for that pale spoke. -> hub
choice Clear light on your page. -> bye
graft @fold resident.hub
choice Can you show me the road on the fold? -> letter_ridge
node letter_ridge
say Fold the paper once, upright like a hill. A cart can have a splendid climb in a drawing that looked completely flat before.
free
choice Can the road come down again? -> letter_flat
choice I'll leave the hill standing. -> hub
node letter_flat
say Press here. Now the same cart has a level journey home. Sometimes I'd like an actual road to take that little account of my wishes.
choice I'd draw a doorway at the end. -> hub
choice I'll travel by the level road. -> bye
